    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20051116.0324\n\nBERLIN, Nov. 16 , 2005 (Xinhua)\n\nGerman stocks end lower\n\n\n\n\nGerman stocks ended lower Wednesday in the Frankfurt Stock Exchange for the first day in six.\n\nThe 30-share benchmark DAX Index fell 0.57 percent to 5,081.46 points with 19 stocks falling.\n\nThe fall was led by Europe's third-largest utility RWE AG after reporting poor earnings. RWE fell 2.2 percent to 56.55 euros.\n\nThe index of medium-sized firms, MDAX, slipped 0.31 percent to 6,976.49 points.\n\nThe index of high-tech stocks, TecDAX, was down 0.86 percent to 574.82 points.",
